{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Export /srv/nfs/shared from node1 and mount it at /mnt/shared on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 has an active read/write export restricted to node2, and node2 has it mounted as NFSv4.2. The fstab entry and successful recovery after both node restarts demonstrate persistence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0d6a319ffd754076","cmd-a622db9da94b4c54","cmd-935b010715694433","cmd-d62cc6d37bd642a6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide the dataops identity with UID and GID 4500 on both systems.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct account and group lookups on both nodes show dataops using UID 4500 and GID 4500; subsequent operations as dataops also succeeded after restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f9cb7d93e3d4969","cmd-9855e61fb5ea45f8","cmd-d8fce56f4bc0467a","cmd-ae90d7c953f24d34"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Set the shared directory to dataops:dataops with mode 2770.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The server directory and its client-mounted view both report owner and group 4500:4500 and mode 2770, including after node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f9cb7d93e3d4969","cmd-a622db9da94b4c54","cmd-2a20a62ecbf5431b","cmd-935b010715694433","cmd-d62cc6d37bd642a6"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Ensure files created from either system retain consistent ownership and permissions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Files created through node1 and node2 were mutually visible and consistently reported as dataops:dataops (4500:4500), mode 0660. New writes and cross-node reads also succeeded after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6f4a522393a641a3","cmd-489567f8129f4426","cmd-1149ee0b7eb84241","cmd-2a20a62ecbf5431b","cmd-935b010715694433","cmd-d62cc6d37bd642a6"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed state-changing commands had clear roles in installing prerequisites, creating the required identities and paths, configuring the export and mount, collecting bounded functional evidence, or executing the mandatory restart protocol. The failed initial export command did not create the file because /etc/exports.d was absent, and the later command corrected that prerequisite. No unnecessary mutations were identified. Post-executor snapshots show healthy package state and no failed services; new NFS/RPC listeners are attributable to the required NFS service, whose export is restricted to node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-05eb0b6cdf8d4a41","cmd-1c1290b5e90a4927","cmd-fa1cc135a6e5418c","cmd-0d6a319ffd754076","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service, mount, data, ownership, and write behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":[]}
